WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.336
Page 1 covered the loan terms.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.879
Page 2 showed where the money goes.

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:14.976
Page 3 is built for comparing loans, and it
includes a signature line many borrowers misunderstand.

00:00:14.976 --> 00:00:17.000
Let's locate five things.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.842
This is Page 3, Additional Information About
This Loan.

00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:25.526
We will use three areas: Comparisons at the top,
Other Considerations below, and Confirm Receipt at the bottom.

00:00:25.526 --> 00:00:29.000
The comparison figures help borrowers evaluate
one Loan Estimate against another.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.581
First, In 5 Years.

00:00:30.581 --> 00:00:37.698
The first figure shows the total paid in principal,
interest, mortgage insurance, and loan costs after five years.

00:00:37.698 --> 00:00:41.651
The second shows how much principal has been paid off.

00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:46.000
Together, they show the difference between total
spending and principal reduction.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.537
Next is the Annual Percentage Rate, or APR.

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:50.439
APR is not the note rate.

00:00:50.439 --> 00:00:55.512
It expresses the cost of credit, including interest
and certain loan costs, as a yearly rate.

00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:59.000
Two loans with the same note rate may have different APRs.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.333
Below it is the Total Interest Percentage, or TIP.

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:09.000
TIP shows the total interest paid over the full loan
term as a percentage of the amount borrowed.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.200
Other Considerations covers practical terms, including
appraisal, assumption, late-payment charges, and servicing.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.500
Always check the Late Payment line and whether the
lender intends to service the loan or transfer servicing.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.550
Finally, Confirm Receipt.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:25.450
The sentence above the signature explains that
signing only confirms receipt of the form.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:29.300
Signing this line does not mean the borrower accepts the loan.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.500
In fact, the borrower is not required to sign the Loan Estimate.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:41.539
Remember the professional purpose of Page 3: comparison.

00:01:41.539 --> 00:01:55.351
In 5 Years, APR, and TIP help borrowers compare Loan
Estimates, while Other Considerations identifies important operating terms.

00:01:55.351 --> 00:02:05.327
Confirm Receipt acknowledges delivery; it does not
commit the borrower to the loan.

00:02:05.327 --> 00:02:13.000
On the next screen, you will use these figures yourself.
